# Line-ending policy for this project's .context_ledger/ directory.
#
# Installed by 'ledger-sync bootstrap'. The vendored core under core/ is
# integrity-checked byte-for-byte against core/MANIFEST.sha256 (LF-computed).
# On Windows with core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF checkout makes every hash
# mismatch and kills the sh manifest parser on '\r'-suffixed filenames.
# Forcing eol=lf keeps the working tree byte-identical to
# the manifest on every platform. Collaboration event files are parsed line by
# line by the sh helpers, so they must stay LF too.
#
# Paths are relative to this .context_ledger/ directory.

# The vendored core: LF, always. Integrity depends on it.
core/**              text eol=lf
core/MANIFEST.sha256 text eol=lf
core/bin/*           text eol=lf

# Project-owned memory: markdown + configs the sh helpers parse.
memory/**            text eol=lf

# Scripts and structured text anywhere under .context_ledger/.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf

# --- Append-only ledger logs: union-merge on conflict --------------------
# These files are append-only — new entries go at the end, past entries are
# never edited — so concurrent sessions and sibling cohorts ALWAYS conflict
# on them at merge time (each branch appended its own rows). git's built-in
# union driver keeps BOTH sides' appended entries and drops the conflict
# markers: the hand recipe ("union the logs") made automatic and identical on
# every platform, so sibling branches merge clean with no per-file surgery.
# After the merge, regenerate the derived digest with `ledger-state reconcile`
# — STATE.md is a derived view and is NOT union-merged (union would corrupt
# it); reconcile regenerates it from the now-merged sources.
memory/office/agents/sessions.md     merge=union
memory/office/flaws/log.md           merge=union
memory/office/inefficiencies/log.md  merge=union
memory/office/plans/decisions.md     merge=union
